  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The existing structure to the front of the\r\nbuilding, by reason of its design, scale and unsympathetic materials, in\r\nconjunction with its prominent siting, results in the overdevelopment of the\r\nsite and constitutes a disproportionate, intrusive, discordant, and incongruous\r\nform of development, to the detriment of the character and visual appearance of\r\nthe existing property and the surrounding area, and harms the positive\r\ncontribution this building made to the setting of the adjacent Edgware High\r\nStreet Conservation Area, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of\r\nthe National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies D3 and HC1 of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021), Core Policies CS1B and CS1D of the Harrow Core Strategy\r\n(2012), Policies DM 1 and DM 7 of the Harrow Development Management Policies\r\nLocal Plan (2013), and the Edgware High Street Conservation Area Appraisal and\r\nManagement Strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
